{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.JetFiltrationGradedDimEscape","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.JetFiltrationGradedDimEscape","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.jet_graded_rho4_exceeds_det_cap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.jet_graded_rho4_exceeds_det_cap","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationGradedDimEscape.lean#L67-L74","doc":"**The escape, stated against the cap constant.** For `q ≥ 1` the\ngraded-dim A=4 ratio strictly exceeds the determinant cap `6 = C(4,2)`\n(`SaturationRhoCap.saturation_rho_cap_four` bounds the `−ln det` ρ₄ by `6`;\nhere the graded ρ₄ is `≥ 12 > 6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.jet_graded_rho4_ge_twelve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.jet_graded_rho4_ge_twelve","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationGradedDimEscape.lean#L51-L65","doc":"**A=4 graded-dim ratio ESCAPES the determinant cap.**\nFor `q ≥ 1`, `ρ_grad(4) = [3]_q · [4]_q ≥ 12 > 6 = C(4,2)`.  So the\njet-filtration graded dimension strictly exceeds the `SaturationRhoCap`\nceiling `saturation_rho_cap_four` proves for the `−ln det` cumulant — it is a\nNON-determinant object that can reach the strong target `ρ_strong(4) ≈ 13.03`\nthe determinant provably cannot.  Equality `= 12` at `q = 1` (`4!/2! = 12`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.jet_graded_rho3_ge_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.jet_graded_rho3_ge_three","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationGradedDimEscape.lean#L43-L49","doc":"**A=3 graded-dim ratio meets the strong regime `> 3`-threshold direction.**\nFor `q ≥ 1`, `ρ_grad(3) = [3]_q ≥ 3`; equality at `q = 1` (the classical\ncoinvariant ratio `3!/2! = 3`).  The strong target `3.81` needs `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.q4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.q4","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationGradedDimEscape.lean#L40-L41","doc":"`[4]_q = 1 + q + q² + q³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.q3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.q3","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/JetFiltrationGradedDimEscape.lean#L37-L38","doc":"`[3]_q = 1 + q + q²`, the `A=3` graded-dimension ratio `W_3/W_2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}